{"id": "wwdc2019-510", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/510", "wordCount": 1052, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hello, and welcome to our"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "session about audio API updates."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "My name is Peter Vasil, and I am"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "a software engineer in the Core"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "Audio team."}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "Let's start with what's new in"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "We have added a couple of"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "enhancements and new APIs to"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "We now have a voice processing"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "support."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "We have added two new nodes,"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "AVAudioSourceNode and"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "AVAudioSinkNode, and we have"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "made some improvements to"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "spatial audio rendering."}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "Now, let's dive into the"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine now has a voice"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "processing mode."}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "The main use case for the mode"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "is echo cancellation and"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "voice-over IP applications."}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "What does this mean?"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "When enabled, extra signal"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "processing is applied on the"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "incoming audio, and any audio"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "that is coming from the device"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "is taken out."}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "This requires that both input"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "and output nodes are in the"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "voice processing mode."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "Therefore, when enabling the"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "mode on either of the I/O nodes,"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "the engine takes care that both"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "I/O nodes exist and that they"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "are switched to the voice"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "processing mode."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "Voice processing is only"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "available when rendering to an"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "audio device, not a manual"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "rendering mode."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "To enable or disable voice"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "processing, we can use set voice"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "processing enabled on either the"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "input or output node."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "Voice processing cannot be"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "enabled dynamically, which means"}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "the engine needs to be in a stop"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "state when enabling the mode."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "The AV Echo Touch Sample Code"}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "project demonstrates how to use"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "voice processing with"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine in detail."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Let's look at the new nodes in"}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine, AVAudioSourceNode"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "and AVAudioSinkNode."}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "Both nodes wrap a user-defined"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "blog that allows apps to send or"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "receive audio from"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "AVAudioEngine."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "When rendering to an audio"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "device, the block operates under"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "real-time constraints, which"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "means that within the block"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "there shouldn't be any blocking"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "calls like memory allocations,"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "call to lib dispatch, or"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "blocking on a mutex."}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "With AVAudioSourceNode, we pass"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "or render block to the node,"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "which sends audio data to its"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "output."}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "This makes it very easy to"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "create generated nodes without"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "having to implement a full audio"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "unit and wrap it with AVAudio"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "unit."}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "The node can be used in both"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "real time and manual rendering"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "mode."}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "AVAudioSourceNode support linear"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "PCM conversions such as sample"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "rate or bit depth conversions"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "and has one output but no input."}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "This short code snippet shows"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "how to use AVAudioSourceNode."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "As we can see, the block is"}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "passed as an initializer"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "argument, and after creating the"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "node, it can be connected just"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "like any other node."}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "A more detailed example can be"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "found in our Signal Generator"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "Sample Code project."}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "Let's look at AVAudioSinkNode."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "AVAudioSinkNode is a symmetrical"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "counterpart of AVAudioSourceNode."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "It wraps a user-defined block"}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "that receives the input audio"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "from the node chain that is"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "connected to its input."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "AVAudioSinkNode is restricted to"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "the input chain."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "In other words, it must be"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "connected downstream of the"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "input node."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "It does not support format"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "conversions, and the format"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "within the block has to be the"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "same as the hardware input"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "format."}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "The node can be useful for"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "voice-over IP application when"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "the input needs to be processed"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "in real time, in which case"}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "installing a regular tap would"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "not be sufficient because the"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "tap doesn't operate in a"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "real-time context."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "Here is a code snippet"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "demonstrating how to create an"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "AVAudioSinkNode."}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "It is quite similar to"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "AVAudioSourceNode."}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "The main steps to note here are"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "to initialize the node with a"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "blog, attach it to the engine,"}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "and connect it to a node"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "downstream of the input node."}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "Now let's see the spatial"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "rendering improvements."}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "We have introduced an automatic"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "spatial rendering algorithm, and"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "AVAudioPlayerNode now supports"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "spatialization of multichannel"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "audio content."}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "With the automatic spatial"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "rendering algorithm, the most"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "appropriate spatialization"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "algorithm is selected for the"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "current route."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "This means developers don't need"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "to figure out what algorithms"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "are suitable for headphones or"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "different speaker configurations."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "This adds near-field and in-head"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "rendering for headphones and"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "virtual surround for built-in"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "speakers is available starting"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "with iOS devices and laptops"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "from 2018 and newer."}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "Here we see the new API in the"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "AVAudio3DMixing protocol."}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "The AVAudio3DMixing rendering"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "algorithm enum has a new entry,"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "auto."}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "Additionally, we can specify the"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "output type with the output type"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "With the property set to auto,"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "the output type can be"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "automatically detected in"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "real-time mode but not in manual"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "rendering mode."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "With the ability to spatialize"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "multichannel streams, we support"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "point-source and ambience bed"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "rendering."}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "We also support channel-based"}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "formats and higher-order"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Ambisonics up to the third"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "order."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "We have added two new"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "spatialization properties to the"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "AVAudio3DMixing protocol, source"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "mode and pointSource and head"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "mode."}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "SpatializeIfMono is legacy"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "behavior."}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "This is the same as bypass for"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "any multichannel stream, which"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "means a pass through or downmix"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "to the output format."}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "With pointSource, the audio is"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "sum to mono and render at the"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "location of the player node."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "And with ambienceBed, the audio"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "is anchored to the 3D world and"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "is rotatable with the player"}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "node's position relative to the"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "listener orientation."}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "Here we see an example of"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "ambienceBed source mode with"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "automatic rendering algorithm."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "After setting the properties, it"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "is important to make sure the"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "format that is used for the"}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "connection between player node"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "and the environment node"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "contains the multichannel"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "layout."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "Now let's talk about what's new"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "in AVAudioSession."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "AVAudioSessionPromptStyle is a"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "hint to apps that play voice"}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "prompts in order to modify the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "style of the played prompt."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "For example, if Siri is speaking"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "or a phone call is ongoing,"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "verbal navigation prompts is a"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "confusing user experience."}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "We also don't want Siri to"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "record a navigation prompt."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Navigation apps, for example,"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "are encouraged to pay attention"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "to prompt style changes and"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "modify the prompts for better"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "user experience."}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "We have three prompt styles,"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "none, short, and normal."}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "We can now indicate to disable"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "prompts completely, play"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "shortened prompts, or play the"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "regular prompts."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "Let's look at other"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "AVAudioSession enhancements."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "The default policy is to mute"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "haptics and system sounds when"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "audio recording is active."}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "A new property, allow haptics"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "and system sounds during"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "recording, allows system sounds"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "and haptics to play while the"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "session is actively using an"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "audio input."}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "It can be set using the"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "setter set allow haptics"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "and system sounds during"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "recording."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "For more information, please"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "visit the developer website."}]}